# Host configuration is a script

When asked to change this machine's configuration, write a script under `tools/` and tell the user the command to run. Do not apply the change yourself.

Host configuration means anything outside the repo that alters the machine: packages, systemd units, NetworkManager, firewalld, BlueZ, udev, polkit, sysctl, groups, and files under `/etc` or the user session.

Inspect the machine if that makes the script correct (`pacman -Q`, `systemctl status`, reading a unit). Stop before the mutating command.

```bash
# BAD — applies the change in the agent session
sudo pacman -S --needed bluez bluez-utils
sudo systemctl enable --now bluetooth.service

# GOOD — tools/enable-bluetooth.sh, then tell the user:
#   ./tools/enable-bluetooth.sh
sudo pacman -S --needed bluez bluez-utils
sudo systemctl enable --now bluetooth.service
```

Match `tools/install_re_toolchain.sh`: `bash`, `set -euo pipefail`, idempotent, a short usage comment. Do not run the new script unless the user asks.
